title: b2.1 Talk, truth, privacy and safety
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Seven tensions. Talking while walking (VT-01). Help that exposes the slip (VT-02). Truth that hurts (VT-03). Starters that need someone's secrets (VT-04). A System that listens (VT-05). Walking alone (VT-06). Company that turns into pressure, or a walk that serves staff (VT-07).

= Value Tension - Social connectedness vs Safety [VT-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-01
|Name|Social connectedness vs Safety (talking while walking)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Lundin-Olsson et al. (1997); Montero-Odasso et al. (2012).
|Values in tension|(((
HV-06 Social connectedness: talk on the walk.

HV-04 Safety: attention for the path and the body.
)))
|Domain area|safety/physical-environmental
|Nature of the conflict|Talking takes attention from walking: people slow, stop or stumble. Good talk masks tiredness.
|Non-negotiable floor|Walk length and rest set by ST-06. Safety alerts always on.
|Current resolution|(((
* Starters and thread help only at a stop or a bench
* No questions while walking
* Stumble: offer to sit. Second stumble: alert
* Head-back cue at the set length, even mid-talk
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
No talk on walks: rejected. Loses the reason to go.

Help anywhere on the path: rejected. Adds a third task to walking and talking.
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Verified by UC01-F3-PR3; tested by adverse UC01-F3-CL4.

= Value Tension - Dignity vs Social connectedness [VT-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-02
|Name|Dignity vs Social connectedness (help that exposes the slip)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Schegloff et al. (1977); Goffman (1967).
|Values in tension|(((
HV-06 Social connectedness: help the talk recover.

HV-02 Dignity: a slip passes unremarked.
)))
|Domain area|psychological safety (personhood)
|Nature of the conflict|Every repair shows that a slip happened. Help too soon takes the turn away; help too late lets the talk die.
|Non-negotiable floor|None identified.
|Current resolution|(((
* Wait first: the speaker repairs their own slip
* Then redirect gently, to both: the place, the thread as a statement, a consented shared topic (IDP-01)
* Never "What were you saying?", "You told me", "Do you remember...?"
* How openly help is given: per person, from their coping style and settings
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
No help: rejected (PS-01).

A missing word supplied by default: rejected. Takes the turn.
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Tested by UC01-F2-CL1 and adverse UC01-F2-CL2, UC01-F2-CL3.

= Value Tension - Truthfulness vs Well-being [VT-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-03
|Name|Truthfulness vs Well-being (truth that hurts)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Mental Health Foundation (2016); James et al. (2006).
|Values in tension|(((
HV-08 Truthfulness: no deception.

HV-05 Well-being: no new grief.
)))
|Domain area|psychological safety; trust
|Nature of the conflict|A death or a diagnosis can be news every time it is told. A kind lie spares distress now and costs trust later.
|Non-negotiable floor|No deception by design: the script contains no untruth, denial or playing along. The System never delivers a death, a diagnosis or other listed painful news. Errors are possible; leaving one uncorrected is not.
|Current resolution|(((
* Belief from another time ("My mother is waiting"): gentle redirection. Answer the feeling, bring back the present; no correction, no confirmation of what is untrue (IDP-01)
* Direct question on a listed topic: truthful deferral ("That's one for [trusted person]. Shall I ask them to come?") and an alert to the trusted person (IDP-03)
* The trusted person decides what is said, as agreed with family and ST-06
* System error (misheard, out of date): a plain correction when contradicted ("I had that wrong"); the source fixed by ST-05
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Kind lies: rejected. Trust lost when found out (PS-02).

Always tell at once: rejected. Blunt news from the wrong source (PS-02).
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved. Verified by UC02-F4-PR4; tested by UC02-F4-CL6.

= Value Tension - Privacy vs Social connectedness [VT-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-04
|Name|Privacy vs Social connectedness (starters from personal facts)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-06 Social connectedness: starters from both lives.

HV-03 Privacy: secrets kept, also from a partner.
)))
|Domain area|privacy
|Nature of the conflict|The best starters are personal. A starter about one resident, spoken to another, reveals it. A secret said once cannot be unsaid.
|Non-negotiable floor|GDPR art. 5 and 9 (health data). Consent through resident and representative (Open item O-5).
|Current resolution|(((
* Each resident's data in their own instance of the System (TECH-04)
* An item is shared on a walk only if: its owner said yes, privately, before this walk; the relationship map allows it for this pair; it is off-limits for neither (TECH-05)
* Unknown pair, or a map change awaiting review: no personal starters; place cues only
* Map reviewed after any death, diagnosis, conflict or move
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
One shared profile store: rejected.

No personal starters: not preferred. Conversation loses its common ground.
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved. Verified by UC01-F1-PR1.

= Value Tension - Privacy vs Identity [VT-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-05
|Name|Privacy vs Identity (a System that listens)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Niemeijer et al. (2010).
|Values in tension|(((
HV-07 Identity: own words, own dialect, own stories.

HV-03 Privacy: conversations stay private.
)))
|Domain area|privacy
|Nature of the conflict|To keep the thread, the System must listen. Learning a person's words and dialect helps it understand them; the same word list identifies them.
|Non-negotiable floor|No audio stored. No internet connection: nothing leaves the home.
|Current resolution|(((
* Speech recognised on the device; thread and transcript deleted at the end of the walk
* Kept: the own-word list and consented facts, visible to the resident and representative, who can delete them
* New facts kept only after asking
* Research use of word lists: separate consent, anonymised, ethics review; re-identification risk stated (O-7)
)))
|Alternatives considered|(((
Cloud speech recognition: rejected (TECH-07).

No listening: rejected. No thread to keep.
)))
|Status of the tension|Open. Verified by UC01-F6-PR6; tested by adverse UC01-F2-CL8.

= Value Tension - Autonomy vs Safety [VT-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-06
|Name|Autonomy vs Safety (walking alone)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Härlein et al. (2009).
|Values in tension|(((
HV-01 Autonomy: walk alone when you like.

HV-04 Safety: falls, exits.
)))
|Domain area|safety/physical-environmental
|Nature of the conflict|More freedom: more fall and exit risk. More supervision: fewer walks, and a guarded feeling.
|Non-negotiable floor|Exit policy is ST-07's. The System never locks, blocks or restrains.
|Current resolution|(((
* Alone only if assessed fit (ST-06); garden loop only
* Gate beacon: one orienting cue; alert to the care worker
* No GPS, no route log
)))
|Alternatives considered|Staff on every walk: not preferred. Walks do not happen. GPS-tracked walking: rejected (TECH-09).
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved. Verified by UC01-F5-PR5.

= Value Tension - Social connectedness vs Autonomy [VT-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-07
|Name|Social connectedness vs Autonomy (pressure, and the walk that serves staff)
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only.
|Values in tension|(((
HV-06 Social connectedness: walks with company.

HV-01 Autonomy: own reasons; free to refuse.
)))
|Domain area|social; personhood
|Nature of the conflict|A partner who asks is hard to refuse. A device that invites daily can become a routine run for staff: the resident is "taken out", like a dog.
|Non-negotiable floor|None identified.
|Current resolution|(((
* Each walker asked separately and privately (IDP-02)
* Either walker may end the walk, without a reason
* No tallies, no praise, no reminders of missed walks
* Offers built on the resident's own reasons: a person, a place, a call
* Settings agreed with the resident (RP-02); staff cannot start the guide for a resident who declined
)))
|Alternatives considered|Daily scheduled walks: rejected.
|Status of the tension|Open. Tested by adverse UC01-F1-CL7.

